bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_af_non_latin_styles_not_ported_2026-11-28, 0, "The autohinter port (src/lib/common/encoding/sfnt_af_latin.spl) has one style: Latin (latn blue strings, standard character o). FreeType picks a style per glyph from its script coverage; every other style still gets the Latin blue zones here. Measured against FreeType light autohint (Liberation Sans Regular, 11 / 13 / 16 px): the superscript style latp (U+00AA U+00B2 U+00B3 U+00B9 U+00BA) differs by 11..91/64 px."
    web_render_af_non_latin_styles_not_ported_2026-11-28, 1, "Missing styles: latp / latb (Latin superscript / subscript: own blue strings), Cyrillic and Greek (own blue strings and standard characters), the fallback for glyphs no script covers, and Devanagari (headline zones; the font-level area gate slo_area in _glyph_outline stands in for it, see web_render_devanagari_latin_blue_zone_hint_2026-11-22 and devanagari_glyph_hint_chrome159_spec). The hinting code itself is shared: a style is a blue string set, a standard character and a coverage range; deva also needs neutral blue zones and top-to-bottom edge order. Until deva exists a font behind the Devanagari gate keeps the old knot hinter (block `Knot hinter: Devanagari-gated fonts only` in sfnt_glyf.spl, about 590 lines): with the Latin port devanagari_mark_position_chrome159_spec fell from 8 of 9 to 6 of 9 (the low u-matra lost its last ink row). Delete that block with the gate."

